# Helpdesk Ticket
# Example Business Knowledge expressed in Menata Language
# Domain: IT/Internal Support — same CMMN-shaped discretionary-task pattern as Case 7's
# Complaint, internal audience instead of external customers
# Case 17 of the Case Portfolio (runtime/case-portfolio.md)
#
# Deliberately light-touch: this is Case 7's Complaint pattern in a different skin
# (internal requester instead of external customer, "Category" instead of "Product
# Quality/Service/Billing"). Written to confirm portability across domains (the same
# proof Case 2 gave Case 1), not because it surfaces anything new.

Ticket

Fields

- Requester : User
- Category : Hardware | Software | Access | Network | Other
- Description : Rich Text
- Priority : Low | Medium | High
- Status : New | Triaged | In Progress | Waiting on Requester | Resolved | Closed | Reopened
- Assigned To : User
- SLA Due Date : Date
- Resolution Notes : Rich Text

Events

When Triage

    SLA Due Date set by Priority

    Status Triaged

When Start Work

    Status In Progress

When Request Info

    Status Waiting on Requester

When Requester Responds

    Status In Progress

When Resolve

    Status Resolved

When Close

    Status Closed

When Reopen

    if Status = Resolved

        Status Reopened

Constraints

- Requester is required.
- Description is required.
- Category is required.

    Resolution Notes is required.

        if Status = Resolved

Permissions

Agent

- Triage
- Start Work
- Request Info
- Resolve

Requester

- Requester Responds
- Reopen

Views

- Ticket Form : Form
- My Tickets : List
- Open Tickets : List
- Ticket Detail : Detail
